## 4. Handoff Review Triggers (`SC14`) & Severity Rubric (`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`)

### Handoff Triggers (`SC14`)
Flag any diff touching these areas in the Code Writer handoff together with the guard that protects it:
- [ ] Authentication, token refresh, session storage, or password/biometric flows (`SC6`, `SC7`)
- [ ] Object-level authorization guards, role/capability checks, or route guards (`SC2`)
- [ ] Data-scope filters, scoped cache keys, or background jobs (`SC3`)
- [ ] File uploads/downloads, deep links, WebViews, or outbound URL calls (`SC5`, `SC9`, `SC10`)
- [ ] New or upgraded dependencies or security linter suppressions (`SC11`)

### Review Severity Rubric (`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`)

| Severity | Security Triggers |
|---|---|
| **`BLOCKER`** | • Missing object-level authorization or data-scope filter (`SC2`, `SC3`)<br>• SQL, command, path, or script injection vector (`SC4`, `SC5`)<br>• Hardcoded secret in source/bundle or plaintext token storage (`SC6`)<br>• Disabled TLS certificate verification in production or fail-open exception catch (`SC9`, `SC13`) |
| **`MAJOR`** | • Unbounded input collection or missing unknown-field rejection at a trust boundary (`SC1`)<br>• Sensitive PII, passwords, or tokens written to logs or exposed in error responses (`SC8`)<br>• Outbound network call without timeout/allow-list or unbounded file upload (`SC9`, `SC10`)<br>• Unpinned or un-audited third-party dependency addition (`SC11`) |
| **`MINOR`** | • Defense-in-depth hardening or missing `SC14` handoff trigger annotation where runtime guards are already present |

